  journal       = "arXiv [cs.CV]",
  abstract      = "Cell painting is a popular technique for creating
                   human-interpretable, high-contrast images of cell morphology.
                   There are two major issues with cell paint: (1) it is
                   labor-intensive and (2) it requires chemical fixation, making
                   the study of cell dynamics impossible. We train a diffusion
                   model (Morphological Observation Neural Enhancement Tool, or
                   MONET) on a large dataset to predict cell paint channels from
