  journal   = "Cancer letters",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  571,
  number    =  216345,
  pages     =  216345,
  abstract  = "Pancreatic cancer is one of the common malignant tumors of the
               digestive system and is known as the ``king of cancers''. It is
               extremely difficult to diagnose at an early stage, the disease
               progresses rapidly, and the effect of chemotherapy and
               radiotherapy is poor, so the prognosis of pancreatic cancer
               patients is very poor. Numerous studies have suggested that
               hypoxia is closely related to the development and progression of
               pancreatic cancer. Inadequate blood supply and desmoplasia in the
               microenvironment of pancreatic cancer can result in its extreme
