  number    =  8,
  pages     = "851--860",
  abstract  = "Single-agent immunotherapy has achieved limited clinical benefit
               to date in patients with pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC).
               This may be a result of the presence of a uniquely
               immunosuppressive tumor microenvironment (TME). Critical
               obstacles to immunotherapy in PDAC tumors include a high number
