               (FAK) activity in neoplastic PDAC cells as an important regulator
               of the fibrotic and immunosuppressive TME. We found that FAK
               activity was elevated in human PDAC tissues and correlated with
               high levels of fibrosis and poor CD8(+) cytotoxic T cell
               infiltration. Single-agent FAK inhibition using the selective FAK
               inhibitor VS-4718 substantially limited tumor progression,
               resulting in a doubling of survival in the
               p48-Cre;LSL-Kras(G12D);Trp53(flox/+) (KPC) mouse model of human
