               survival and identify aggressive tumors among transcriptionally
               discordant cases. PanSubNet enables molecular subtyping directly
               from routine histology and provides a rapid, tissue-sparing
               complement to transcriptomic profiling. This approach may broaden
               access to biologically informed stratification, particularly when
               molecular testing is limited or impractical. Pancreatic cancer
               can be divided into biological groups that may differ in how
