  journal  = "GigaScience",
  volume   =  6,
  number   =  2,
  pages    = "1--11",
  abstract = "BACKGROUND: Phosphorylation is the most frequent
              post-translational modification made to proteins and may regulate
              protein activity as either a molecular digital switch or a
              rheostat. Despite the cornucopia of high-throughput (HTP)
              phosphoproteomic data in the last decade, it remains unclear how
