  pages     = "924--938",
  abstract  = "Although patient-derived xenografts (PDX) are commonly used for
               preclinical modeling in cancer research, a standard approach to
               in vivo tumor growth analysis and assessment of antitumor
               activity is lacking, complicating the comparison of different
               studies and determination of whether a PDX experiment has
               produced evidence needed to consider a new therapy promising. We
