              tumor tissue as a genomically, transcriptomically, and
              functionally similar tumor source compared to the standard,
              manually excised remnant tumor sample approved by clinical
              pathology. Collecting this often-discarded tumor source increased
              the mass of tumors accrued by nearly 5-fold and enabled collection
              from 11 additional patients, significantly increasing tumor tissue
              for downstream testing on SLiCE. These findings establish SLiCE as
              a scalable, clinically relevant platform for FPM in brain cancer,
